ink now for the first time  unfortunately it's taken so long but for  the first time the european union with  the leaders meeting today will deal with  the problem of the refugee camps  bordering Syria the frontline States  they also need to deal with the Balkan  states went through which the refugees  have been moving and they need some  assistance they need to put this quota  system in place and then they have to  deal with the last point that we're  talking about about integrating the  refugees into the country's once once  they are located wherever they end up  being located wrong so it's a huge  challenge huge challenge Angela Merkel  had said this crisis makes the eurozone  crisis as important as it was pale in  comparison right well thank you so much  for being here with us ok for more  information about professor Cameron and  his research please visit our website at  macmillan report yale edu be sure to  join us again for another episode of the  macmillan report made possible through  funding from the Whitney and Betty  Macmillan Center for International and  area studies at Yale
 

